{"term":"accord","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5792d69a5eba8e2df0","definition":"Agreement of opinion, will, or action.","example":"These all continued with one accord in prayer and supplication, with the women, and Mary the mother of Iesus, and with his brethen.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["consent","assent"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["in accord","of one's own accord","with one accord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5a41930529c62ea3a3","definition":"Agreement in pitch and tone; harmony, musical concord.","example":"Those sweet accords are even the angels' lays.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["in accord","of one's own accord","with one accord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be53854ca5d7c23b23","definition":"Agreement or harmony of things in general.","example":"the accord of light and shade in painting","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["in accord","of one's own accord","with one accord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f34e582bc963eaeded","definition":"A distinctive mixture of fragrances or the odor thereof.","example":"Oriental fragrances often incorporate an accord referred to as amber. It is a perfumery accord using vanilla, olibanum, balsamic resins, and citrus to varying degrees.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["in accord","of one's own accord","with one accord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d3a332dbeeeb273181","definition":"An agreement between parties in controversy, by which satisfaction for an injury is stipulated, and which, when executed, prevents a lawsuit.","example":"Accord is a satisfaction agreed upon between the party injuring and the party injured ; which , when performed , is a bar of all actions upon this account","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["in accord","of one's own accord","with one accord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4d612e28df275f3ff9","definition":"An international agreement.","example":"The Geneva Accord of 1954 ended the French-Indochinese War.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["treaty"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["in accord","of one's own accord","with one accord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:35260a87182b9bf972","definition":"Voluntary or spontaneous impulse to act.","example":"Nobody told me to do it. I did it of my own accord.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["in accord","of one's own accord","with one accord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"k